(DocMind Executive Summary: Table-Aware Ingestion and Retrieval Upgrade) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Overview) Tj
T*
(DocMind was upgraded from a text-only retrieval flow toward a table-aware architecture.) Tj
T*
(The goal was to make financial, comparative, and tabular questions more reliable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key Changes Delivered) Tj
T*
(1. Added page-level table detection for every PDF page with configurable thresholds.) Tj
T*
(2. Integrated Camelot extraction with validation, markdown conversion, and numeric normalization.) Tj
T*
(3. Added dedicated document_tables storage plus page detections and extraction failure logs.) Tj
T*
(4. Introduced one unified embeddings layer for text blocks, full tables, and row-level table entries.) Tj
T*
(5. Replaced the old per-upload background thread with a queue-backed async worker flow.) Tj
T*
(6. Persisted original PDF bytes so async workers can process the source document after upload.) Tj
T*
(7. Enriched tables with provenance such as page number, bounding box, and nearby heading or caption.) Tj
T*
(8. Updated retrieval so search can return hydrated table evidence, including highlighted rows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Business Impact) Tj
T*
(The platform now has a reliable foundation for numeric lookup, year-over-year comparison,) Tj
T*
(and future LLM answer generation over structured document tables.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Current Boundary) Tj
T*
(The ask route still returns top evidence directly. Groq-based answer synthesis was left for the next phase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Verification Note) Tj
T*
(Code changes were implemented in the workspace and retrieval tests were updated.) Tj
T*
(Executable verification was partially blocked because this machine does not expose a working Python launcher) Tj
T*
(and the checked-in virtual environment points to a missing interpreter.) Tj
T*
